   "subject": "Re: ppmc issues - Mu.hat",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div><div>Charles,</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for this report and welcome to blavaan. This is a bug that will be fixed. </div><div><br></div><div>To work around the issue, you can add meanstructure=TRUE to your bcfa() command:</div><div><br></div><div>fit &lt;- bcfa(HS.model, data = HolzingerSwineford1939, n.chains = 2, burnin = 1000, sample = 500, meanstructure = TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>It doesn&#39;t change the model in any way, it just ensures that there is a mean vector for the ppmc() command.</div><div><br></div><div>Ed</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>On Tue, 2023-02-14 at 12:19 -0500, Charles Hofacker wrote:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:2px #729fcf solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div>When I run the (single group) analysis shown in the ppmc() help file,</div><div><br></div><div>HS.model &lt;- &#39; visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3</div><div>              textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6</div><div>              speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9 &#39;</div><div>## fit single-group model</div><div>fit &lt;- bcfa(HS.model, data = HolzingerSwineford1939,</div><div>            n.chains = 2, burnin = 1000, sample = 500)</div><div>AFIs &lt;- ppmc(fit, thin = 10, fit.measures = c(&quot;srmr&quot;,&quot;chisq&quot;,&quot;rmsea&quot;,&quot;cfi&quot;))</div><div><br></div><div>I see the following: </div><div><br></div><div>Error in 1:nrow(Mu.hat[[g]]) : argument of length 0</div><div><br></div><div>I am using R4.2.0 and blavaan 0.4-6. </div><div><br></div><div>Am really just getting started using blavaan so who knows what shenanigans I have got myself into! </div><div>__________________________________________________________________</div><div>Charles Hofacker: Facebook | Google Scholar | Twitter</div></blockquote></div>"
