   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">That did the trick! It also solved something that had confused me, namely that the LVs were all coming out as NA. Now that I think about it, it is easy to imagine that augmenting the draws with the latent variables would depend in some way on means. <div><br></div><div>From my point of view it is pretty amazing to have a direct line of communication to the developer! I learned frequentist SEM/CFA kind of a long time ago. I don&#39;t want to age myself but let&#39;s just say that the ACOVS program was about all there was out there when I was first introduced to this stuff in grad school. </div><div><br></div><div>I have been converting to Bayesian inference and just having a lot of fun. </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks! </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
